---
import SourcePanel from '../components/SourcePanel.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../data/assets';
import { SOURCES } from '../data/sources';

const title = 'Grave Seasons Tips - Spoiler-Safe Pre-Launch Planning';
const description =
  'Spoiler-safe Grave Seasons tips based on confirmed systems: autosaved decisions, the 24-hour clock, farming plot types, the roguelike mines, residents, and changing killers.';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Tips', url: '/tips/' },
];
const sources = [SOURCES.steam, SOURCES.steamDevlog, SOURCES.blumhouse];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} image={ASSETS.farmHarvest.src}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="section-kicker">Pre-launch tips</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-bone md:text-5xl">
      Grave Seasons Tips
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fog">
      Grave Seasons launches on March 9, 2027, so nobody outside the studio has tested crop prices or murder schedules
      yet. These tips are built only on systems the Steam page and the developer's devlogs have confirmed. Each one
      links to the page with the full detail.
    </p>

    <figure class="mt-8">
      <img src={ASSETS.farmHarvest.src} alt={ASSETS.farmHarvest.alt} width={ASSETS.farmHarvest.width} height={ASSETS.farmHarvest.height} class="rounded-md border border-white/10" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">{ASSETS.farmHarvest.credit}</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="prose-page mt-8">
      <h2>Spoiler-safe starter advice</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Track your decisions.</strong> Steam says decisions are checked and autosaved, so assume important
          branches may not be easy to undo. Write down the choice and the date before you see the result.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Treat time as your scarcest resource.</strong> The Day &amp; Night Cycle devlog describes a full
          24-hour clock with no hard bedtime, and says time keeps ticking whatever you do. Late nights are useful for
          investigating, but they cost you rest you need for farming. See the <a href="/day-and-night/">day and night guide</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Learn the three plot types before planting big.</strong> The farming devlog names Arid, Regular, and
          Wet plots, and says Wet plots do not need watering. It also confirms four seasons and more than 45 seeds,
          but no prices or growth times. Start with a small test plot. The <a href="/farming-grid-seasons-guide/">farming grid guide</a> has the rest.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Prepare before you go into the mines.</strong> The November 4, 2026 devlog says the mines are
          roguelike with generated levels and no enemies; the pressure comes from your time and energy, and it grows
          the deeper you go. Bring supplies and set a turnaround point. Details are in the <a href="/mines-roguelike-preview/">mines preview</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Watch every resident, at every hour.</strong> Steam confirms 30+ residents and a killer chosen from a
          pool of candidates, and the devlog says residents keep schedules at night as well. A short note per resident
          beats memory; the <a href="/killer-decisions-and-replay/">investigation notes guide</a> gives a template.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Do not treat a romance as a safe answer.</strong> Steam lists 12 potential romance options and says a
          few may be the killer. Keep relationship notes separate from your suspect notes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Record season and location.</strong> Steam says changing seasons affect the world around you and lists
          seven major areas, from your farm to the mines. What you see in spring may not be there in winter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Expect a different case next time.</strong> Each playthrough selects a killer with its own reasoning,
          kill style, and targets. Label notes by run so a second playthrough does not overwrite the first.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Using the controller on the farm</h2>
      <p>
        The September 30, 2026 launch-date post mentions two controller changes made for the console versions: a radial
        menu and a hold-to-rotate input for working on farming plots. If you plan to play with a pad, spend your first
        few minutes facing a plot and rotating in place to see which tile is selected. The
        <a href="/controller-and-crowbar-gameplay-preview/">controller and crowbar preview</a> goes further.
      </p>

      <h2>What to avoid before launch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Crop profit charts, best-gift lists, or murder schedules posted before March 9, 2027. None of that data is public.</li>
        <li>"Free download", demo, or APK sites. There is no public build; see <a href="/demo-status/">demo status</a>.</li>
        <li>Killer identities presented as fixed. The killer changes between playthroughs, so a single "answer" cannot apply to everyone.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For a fuller first-year plan that ties these tips together, read the
        <a href="/grave-seasons-prelaunch-one-year-planner/">one-year planner</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <SourcePanel sources={sources} />
  </article>
</Layout>
